From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:05:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: share tracked VM lifetime and native query support

Share tracked GPUVM lifetime, native query support and CPU-retired
timestamp mappings with the G16 backend. Close unpublished VMs on
allocation failure and release backend handle owners on close, while
accepted jobs retain their own leases. Complete page-table rollback under
PPL, then invalidate after dropping the handoff mutex. Keep legacy backend
behavior and compile with G16 disabled and WERROR enabled.

Generated-by: Codex
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
[ryan: rebased onto 7.3 integration/aurora; the G16 SGX mapping uses
DevresIoMem, file open keeps the memacct client, and gem_create admits
the memacct commit before prepare_new_object; held_sg_table()
returns a must-use SG table, which the CPU timestamp path drops]
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
[dylan: most of this change is already in omacom through its own Aurora
 ports (the merge result equals omacom for gpu.rs, file.rs, mmu.rs,
 mmu/, queue/, regs.rs, timestamp.rs and g17/), so only the G16 hooks
 are added. omacom gates the adopted-UAT code in mmu.rs with
 CONFIG_DRM_ASAHI_UAT_ADOPTION rather than CONFIG_DRM_ASAHI_G16;
 DRM_ASAHI_G16 selects it in the G16 backend commit. asahi_core.rs keeps
 the G15 module and registration and registers G16 before the infallible
 G15 activation. driver.rs keeps the M3 runtime field next to the G16
 one in every platform data literal; Drop is unchanged (G16 keeps its
 firmware state until reboot, as in aurora). file.rs keeps omacom's
 gpu.feature_flags(), which already covers VM status, independent queues
 and soft faults, and the one-argument gem::prepare_new_object(); gem.rs
 gains a G16-only variant of it that takes the held SG table through the
 GEM's bound device, as G15 does. pgtable.rs: leaf_bits() is also built
 for G16.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
